mmc: sdhci-sprd: the ZTE V50's eMMC host kept awake (FINDINGS 95)

On a ZTE V50 (MU3351, the F50's platform) under mainline, kano (kanoqwq, his line of this project, 2026-10-14) saw
ext4 report "deleted inode referenced": directory entries of inodes already deleted, after normal reboots, back again
after an offline fsck. What he changed and measured on his V50: the non-removable eMMC host's runtime PM forbidden
at probe, before its first autosuspend (kernel 7.2.8 "#17": power/control "on", runtime_status "active"); a marker,
the configuration and the scripts then survived a sync and a normal reboot with their SHA-256, and ext4's
errors_count was 0. In his words an improvement, not proof that runtime PM alone caused it. Writing power/control
"on" from the initramfs instead was tried and hung the boot before the mount, so it is the driver's to do.

Only on the V50: it is told by its AW9523B LED controller ("awinic,aw9523b"), which neither the F50's nor the U30
Air's device tree has (both read: no such node), so on those this is a lookup that finds nothing. The V50 has no
battery; the cost is the host's idle power. The card slot is never affected.

A separate patch: the trees prepared with 0001-0016 take it as it is.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-sprd.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-sprd.c
@@ -747,6 +747,23 @@
 	return false;
 }
 
+/*
+ * MU300: the ZTE V50's eMMC host is never runtime-suspended. On a V50 under mainline, ext4 found directory entries
+ * of deleted inodes after reboots, again after an fsck; with its host kept awake from probe on (before the first
+ * autosuspend) the data survived a reboot (kano, 2026-10-14; FINDINGS 95). The V50 is told by its AW9523B LED
+ * controller, which no F50's or U30 Air's device tree has: on those nothing changes. It has no battery to save.
+ */
+static bool sdhci_sprd_keep_awake(struct sdhci_host *host)
+{
+	struct device_node *np;
+
+	if (mmc_card_is_removable(host->mmc))
+		return false;
+	np = of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "awinic,aw9523b");
+	of_node_put(np);
+	return np;
+}
+
 static int sdhci_sprd_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct sdhci_host *host;
@@ -865,6 +882,10 @@
 	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(&pdev->dev, 50);
 	pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_suspend_ignore_children(&pdev->dev, 1);
+	if (sdhci_sprd_keep_awake(host)) {
+		pm_runtime_forbid(&pdev->dev);
+		dev_info(&pdev->dev, "MU300: ZTE V50, eMMC host kept awake\n");
+	}
 
 	sdhci_enable_v4_mode(host);
 
@@ -911,6 +932,8 @@
 	sdhci_cleanup_host(host);
 
 pm_runtime_disable:
+	if (sdhci_sprd_keep_awake(host))
+		pm_runtime_allow(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_put_noidle(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_set_suspended(&pdev->dev);
